// `json.parse::<T>` is still rejected at check time when `T` has no JSON decoding. A *payload-free*
// enum decodes now (see `enums/decode_plain_enum_field`), so the undecodable shape this pins is an
// enum with a **payload-carrying** variant: a data-carrying sum has no canonical JSON spelling, and
// decoding only its payload-free half would accept documents against a schema that cannot describe
// the type — so the enum declines as a whole. Such a case is built by `construct("Shape.Circle", […])`
// instead, where the payload is named data rather than a guessed encoding.
// A compile-time E0007, so both backends agree (the program never runs).
// expect: error E0007 at 11:5
use std.{json};
enum Shape { Dot; Circle(r: int); }
c = json.parse::<Shape>("\"Dot\"");
echo c;
